{#-
  Cisco IOS / IOS-XE -- NAC on access ports.

  ============================ REVIEW THIS BLOCK ============================
  This is a generic IBNS 2.0 access-port configuration, not your standard.
  Correct it to match what your access ports should look like and the audit
  follows automatically -- there is nothing else to change.

  If your fleet is still on legacy `authentication ...` commands rather than
  `access-session ...`, replace the block wholesale; the commented lines at the
  bottom are the legacy equivalents.
  ===========================================================================

  How it is used: the planner renders this once in `declare` mode to learn what
  a compliant port looks like, compares every in-scope port against it, and
  renders it again as `interface X` plus only the lines that port is missing.
  One copy of the standard, and it is the one that gets pushed.

  Available variables:
    declare  bool                 emit the required block, with no interface
    add      list[str]            interfaces to correct
    missing  {interface: [lines]} what each of them lacks
    policy   str|None             subscriber control policy name
-#}
{% if declare %}
switchport mode access
access-session host-mode multi-auth
access-session closed
access-session port-control auto
mab
dot1x pae authenticator
dot1x timeout tx-period 7
{% if policy %}
service-policy type control subscriber {{ policy }}
{% endif %}
spanning-tree portfast
spanning-tree bpduguard enable
{#-
  Legacy IBNS 1.0 equivalents, for a fleet not yet migrated:
    authentication host-mode multi-auth
    authentication order dot1x mab
    authentication priority dot1x mab
    authentication port-control auto
    authentication periodic
    authentication timer reauthenticate server
    authentication violation restrict
-#}
{% else %}
{% for name in add %}
interface {{ name }}
{% for line in missing[name] %}
 {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
